{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's sensor and actuator interface, separating perception and motion. The specification encodes a safe, coverage-oriented supervisor: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery from obstacles uses directed turns or, as a last resort, a full scan. All obstacle events force a recovery turn before returning to exploration. The design ensures determinism, avoids oscillation, and prevents forward/coverage actions in unsafe states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to clarify uncontrollable vs controllable event domains.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward for short progress, directed turn recovery for obstacles, and full_rotate only as a last-resort escape."
